1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Edward Thompson (1929-2017) was a commercial fire inspector for ADT.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary:
2 CONT Edward C. Thompson, 88, of Pennington passed away Tuesday May 23rd at Brandywine Assisted Living. Born in Jersey City, New Jersey, he retired from ADT where he was a Commercial Fire Inspector. Edward was a member of the IBEW Union
2 CONC  #2 for over 60 years. He was a Navy veteran serving during the Korean War where he was Seaman First Class. Son of the late Trygve A. Thompson and Clara Schultz Thompson, he is survived by his wife Teresa Marie Halleran Thompson, 
2 CONC his son and daughter-in-law, Mark and Sue Thompson of Pennington, 2 daughters, Karen Anderson of Charlotte, North Carolina and Barbara Thompson of Pinehurst, North Carolina, 4 grandchildren, Christina Thompson, Mark Thompson II, K
2 CONC evin Thompson and Casey Anderson. Graveside services were held Thursday May 25th 11:00 a.m. at Whiting Memorial Park Mausoleum, 600 County Road 530, Manchester Twp., New Jersey 08759. There will be no calling hours. Arrangements a
2 CONC re by the Wilson-Apple Funeral Home, 2560 Pennington Road, Pennington, New Jersey.
