1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Donald A. Extrom of Schaumburg for 40 years Services for Donald A. Extrom, 73, will begin with prayers at 9:30 a.m. Tuesday, Nov. 17, at Michaels Funeral Home, 800 S. Roselle Road (between Higgins and Irving Park R
2 CONC oad), Schaumburg, proceeding to Lord of Life Lutheran Church, Schaumburg, for memorial services at 10 a.m. Visitation will be from 3 to 9 p.m. Monday, Nov. 16, at the funeral home. Born Dec. 21, 1935, in Hinsdale, he passed away p
2 CONC eacefully at home Saturday, Nov. 14, 2009, surrounded by his family. Donald was valedictorian of Downers Grove High School in 1954, and was a fantastic athlete lettering in both basketball and baseball. He worked at U.S. Life Insu
2 CONC rance Company for over 40 years and became senior vice president of operations. He was the adoring husband for 47 years of Karen (nee Nelson); loving father of Mark (Colleen), Ann Marie Redden and John; fond grandfather of Samanth
2 CONC a, James, Brittany and Corey Redden and Lilli; and dear brother of Richard. In lieu of flowers, donations may be made in Donald's name to Lord of Life Lutheran Church, 847-895-8877. For further information, please call 847-891-290
2 CONC 0 or visit www.michaelsfh.com. - See more at: http://m.legacy.com/obituaries/dailyherald/obituary
