0 @I6000000184916712840@ INDI
1 NAME Barbara Ann /Thompson/
2 GIVN Barbara Ann
2 SURN Thompson
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 16 FEB 1962
2 ADDR
3 CITY Ridgefield
3 STAE NJ
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 17 JUN 2019
2 ADDR
3 CITY Pinehurst
3 STAE NC
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Barbara Ann Thompson (1962-2019)
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary:
2 CONT Barbara Thompson, 57, of Pinehurst, passed away Monday, June 17, 2019, at First Health Hospice House in Pinehurst. Born February 16, 1962, Barbara attended schools in Ridgefield, New Jersey, and graduated from Ridgefield Memorial 
2 CONC High School in 1980. She was a long-time employee of Panasonic, both in New Jersey and in Southern California, where she lived for 12 years. Barbara resided in Central New Jersey from 2000 through 2005, and then moved to Pinehurst
2 CONC  with her husband Tom. She loved life in Pinehurst, the tranquility of the area, friendliness of the residents, the close proximity of family including her parents, and the many good friends at the Village, where she worked for 12
2 CONC  years. These friends loved and supported Barbara during her struggle with cancer. Predeceased by her husband Tom DellaRossa and her father Edward Thompson, Barbara is survived by her mother, Teresa; brother, Mark; and sister, Kar
2 CONC en; two nieces and two nephews; and many close friends in Pinehurst. Her beloved golden retrievers, Hunter and Ryder, are now broken-hearted. Barbara fought cancer for close to two years, with determination, steadfast optimism, sm
2 CONC iles, and a goal of being home. Later this summer, she will return to New Jersey to be with the remains of Tom and her first dog, Caymen. There will be a celebration of Barbara’s life at that time. Donations in her honor can be ma
2 CONC de to The American Cancer Society or the Neuse River Golden Retriever Rescue.
